1:47:021 Stunde, 47 Minuten, 2 Sekundenstages of sleep, the phalamus, that relay station deep in the center of the brain that roots sensory information up
1:47:101 Stunde, 47 Minuten, 10 Sekundento the cortex, begins to change its firing pattern. During waking life, phthalamic neurons fire in what's called
1:47:181 Stunde, 47 Minuten, 18 Sekundena tonic mode, a steady, reliable relay of information, passing signals faithfully from your eyes, your ears,
1:47:271 Stunde, 47 Minuten, 27 Sekundenyour skin up to the cortical areas that make sense of them. But as sleep pressure builds, those same neurons
