How does your brain turn electrical signals, memories, and sensory information into the reality you experience?

This video explores the fascinating science of how the brain constructs our perception of the world — from the way our senses collect information to how the brain interprets sights, sounds, touch, and other signals. We look at how perception is shaped by attention, expectations, memories, and the brain’s constant attempts to predict what is happening around us.

We also explore illusions, unconscious processing, and why what we experience as reality is not simply a perfect recording of the outside world, but something the brain continuously builds and updates.
A slow journey through perception, consciousness, and the remarkable processes that create your experience of reality.

